  "review_notes": [
    "The original record has a genuinely dependent euler : EulerCharacteristic complex and a genuine integer inequality euler.value !=0, together with supplied arithmetic data and an independent arbitrary complexRealizesLFunction proposition/proof. Both projection proofs are actual source proof content.",
    "The inspected EulerCharacteristic provider stores an Int value with an unlinked value_eq_signed_sum proposition; SectionComplex stores a degreewise function and independent d_comp_d_zero and bounded propositions. Do not infer an actual Euler sum, chain-complex equation, cohomology construction or topological anchor from those names.",
    "CertifiedBaseCaseEllipticCurve carries arbitrary data types, optional arithmetic contracts, supplied L-function/normalization packages and a supplied nonvanishing proposition. Optional contracts need not be Some. Actual BSD equalities and normalization equalities in inspected contexts are acknowledged, without inventing relations to this supplied integer.",
    "Keep the mixed original own-provider structure and both genuine proofs in exact GRWTSK archives. Splitting its fields would change the type, and extracting its proof would require maintaining the whole mixed interface or inventing a new legacy provider import."
  ],
